udents which you know exceeds the  total number of students in the school  which tells me that there must be some  overlap between these two sets it would  be this type of scenario right here but  the question is is you know how much of  an overlap is there well again when we  add these together 100 and 120 that  comes out to a total of 220  which exceeds  you know the number of students in the  school by 20. so it looks like that at a  minimum there's going to need to be an  overlap of 20 students in this region  right here so the answer would be  20 students so again something to just  refresh your memory on and that's just  this concept of venn diagrams  and meaning you know intersection or the  overlap or meaning the union you're  combining both sets together but you  don't want to double count the ones that  are in both groups so definitely  important something something important  to understand for the act and i'll see  you in the next lesson
 

